{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact flush-fix head 17b8d5e91d151893c56284564b1ee143bbdd2050 on builder/receive-pack-flush-20261103, tree 5145da7b, for request 662dbc1f under promise a612b9ea and review request a7c33307. This approval covers the parser change in SmartHttpGit.send and its tests. It claims no deployment, no fresh G3 witness and no G3 acceptance.\n\nScope. Main 331bf5f2 is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. Against main, the head changes packages/git/src/http.ts, packages/git/test/http.test.ts, the note and three manifests. cc6c1c15 merges landed O3 and adds nothing else. The commit-message check passes for all four commits. No card path changes.\n\nThe boundary holds:\n\n- packets still reads the whole body. It throws on a non-hex length, a length of 1 to 4, a packet that overruns the body, or a body that does not end in a flush. Trailing data therefore never parses.\n- send now accepts three or four records only. Record 3 must be a flush, and a fourth record must also be a flush. Then the unpack line and the exact own-ref status decide the answer, as before. The old rule never checked that record 3 was a flush, so the new rule is also stricter there.\n- The positive case builds synthetic ASCII from the diagnosis's public layout: 14 and 54 bytes, then flushes at 68 and 72, for 76 bytes. It confirms only with the exact read-back. A different read-back stays unknown.\n- Six named refusals cover two extra flushes, trailing data, a missing flush, a wrong ref, a status for another ref and an extra unpack line. Each reaches one POST and stays unknown.\n- Control 03 restores the three-record limit, and the observed-layout case fails. Control 04 removes the interior flush check, and the foreign-status case fails. That case uses one flush, so the length rule alone cannot catch it. Both controls restore the source.\n- The note answers the hosted question. Hosted Workers that publish to GitHub and celld both reach this parser through GitHubProvider.send and sendOnce. A mini-only deployment therefore leaves the hosted Workers on the old rule.\n\nThe gate. Ruling 6500f198 asks me to judge the sealed record, and it is enough for this change. gate.exit at cc6c1c15 reads exit 1, and the gate stays failed on the record. My reasons:\n\n- Every stage's cases pass: Node 133, Counting 56, plain 3,601 with one skip, and Native 1,060 with two skips. The plain count is seven more than gate 4 of O3 found at 07af767b: the one positive and the six refusals.\n- The only failure is one EnvironmentTeardownError in a vitest worker, which names packages/scope/test/archive-input.test.ts. No case in that file fails.\n- Against main, the source differs only by six lines of synchronous comparison in http.ts. O3's Native follow-up ran the same Native suite on main's source with zero unhandled errors, so this change cannot plausibly start the pending call.\n- source-before and source-after both record cc6c1c15, tree 1536e493 and a clean status. The named file alone passes both cases with exit 0 at the same head.\n- Request df2abe35 tracks the teardown race. Until it lands, the same error can fail any gate.\n\nEvidence. The three manifests hash to a24019a5…, fcf103e4… and 113febc9…, as the request states. All 22 public files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, every SHA256SUMS file matches, and no unit holds an unlisted file. All 39 private files match their indexes. The scan for private keys, GitHub tokens and bearer values finds no match.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The fix stays in the one parser, and the caller's exact read-back still decides acceptance.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. A reply can now carry one more flush and nothing else. Every malformed reply still stays unknown, and no reply is accepted without the read-back.\n\nSimplification: no required change.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f59218f3b99fc763d97e6a2c3956ee2642bae0d7","binding":"assigned","head":"17b8d5e91d1